---
// DRAFT for counsel review (PRD V-10). Keep `noindex` and keep this page out
// of the sitemap until the owner confirms legal review is complete.
// Keep the provider list in step with what the site and the Worker actually
// use (wrangler.jsonc, scripts/security-headers.mjs, worker/).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalDraft from '../components/LegalDraft.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
const UPDATED = 'October 22, 2026';
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="What personal information Benjaire collects, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept and the rights you have over it." noindex>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">What we collect, why we collect it, who we share it with and the choices you have.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We collect only what you give us (an inquiry, an order or a booking) and the basic technical data needed to run and protect the site.</li>
        <li>We don't sell your personal information, share it for targeted advertising or use advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>Trusted providers such as Cloudflare, Stripe and Calendly handle it for us, only to deliver our services.</li>
        <li>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information at any time by emailing <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>{SITE.legalName} ("Benjaire", "we", "us") is a New York limited liability company and is responsible for the personal information described here. This policy covers benjaire.com, the inquiries you send us, purchases of Benjaire Flow and calls you book with us. Each Benjaire brand operates its own website with its own privacy policy.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>Information you give us</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inquiries.</strong> When you use the contact form or email us: your name, email address, company (if you add one), the inquiry category you choose and your message.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchases.</strong> When you buy Benjaire Flow: your name, email address, billing address, what you bought, the amount, tax and the date. Stripe collects your card or other payment details directly. We never see or store your full card number.</li>
        <li><strong>Bookings.</strong> When you book a call through Calendly: your name, email address, the time you choose and any answers you add to the booking form.</li>
        <li><strong>Support and setup.</strong> What you tell us during setup calls and support emails. For Flow Installed, we work inside accounts you own with access you grant us, and we don't copy your clients' data out of them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Information collected automatically</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Request data.</strong> Like every website, ours receives your IP address, browser type, device type, the pages you request and the referring page. Cloudflare processes this to deliver the site and block attacks. We use your IP address briefly to limit how often forms can be sent.</li>
        <li><strong>Spam protection.</strong> The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks browser signals to tell people from bots. It doesn't use advertising cookies or track you across sites.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitor statistics.</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics counts page views without cookies and without building a profile of you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Cookies and similar technology</strong></p>
      <p>We don't set advertising or tracking cookies, and we don't run third-party ad or social media pixels. Turnstile may use strictly necessary technical data to work. The booking calendar loads only when you choose to open it, and Calendly may then set its own cookies under its own policy.</p>

      <h2>How we use it, and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To answer your inquiry</strong> and manage any business relationship that follows. We do this because you asked us to, and it's in our legitimate interest to reply.</li>
        <li><strong>To process orders, deliver Benjaire Flow, provide support and handle refunds.</strong> We need this to perform our contract with you.</li>
        <li><strong>To schedule and hold calls you book.</strong> This performs our agreement with you.</li>
        <li><strong>To keep the site secure</strong> and prevent spam, fraud and abuse. This is our legitimate interest and yours.</li>
        <li><strong>To understand which pages are visited</strong>, in total, so we can improve the site. This is our legitimate interest, using cookieless statistics.</li>
        <li><strong>To keep records and meet legal obligations</strong>, such as tax, accounting and responding to lawful requests.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't use your information for advertising, and we only send you marketing email if you ask for it. Every marketing email lets you unsubscribe.</p>

      <h2>AI-assisted sorting</h2>
      <p>Messages sent through our contact form are read by Anthropic's Claude AI model, which suggests a category, urgency and a draft reply for our team. A person at Benjaire reviews every inquiry and decides how to respond. Claude doesn't reply to you on its own or make any decision with legal or similarly significant effects on you. Under Anthropic's commercial terms, this data isn't used to train its models.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We share personal information only with service providers that process it on our behalf, under contracts that limit how they may use it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> website hosting, security, spam protection (Turnstile), email routing and cookieless visitor statistics.</li>
        <li><strong>n8n:</strong> runs our inquiry workflow, which stores contact form messages so we can track and answer them.</li>
        <li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> AI sorting of contact form messages, as described above.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend:</strong> sends our acknowledgement, welcome and delivery emails from contact@benjaire.com.</li>
        <li><strong>Our email inbox provider:</strong> stores the emails you send us and our replies.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe:</strong> payments, tax calculation, receipts and fraud prevention. Stripe also acts as an independent controller for some payment data; see <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Stripe's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendly:</strong> scheduling calls you book with us; see <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Calendly's Privacy Notice</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information when the law requires it, to protect our rights or the safety of others, or to a buyer or successor if Benjaire's business is ever sold or reorganized, in which case this policy continues to apply.</p>

      <h2>We don't sell or share your information</h2>
      <p>We don't sell personal information, and we don't share it for cross-context behavioral advertising, as those terms are defined under California law. We haven't done so in the past 12 months. We honor Global Privacy Control signals as an opt-out request, even though there is nothing to opt out of.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inquiries and booking details:</strong> up to 24 months after our last contact, unless an ongoing business relationship needs them longer.</li>
        <li><strong>Order records</strong> (what you bought, when, the amount and tax): as long as tax and accounting law requires, generally up to seven years.</li>
        <li><strong>Request and security logs:</strong> kept briefly by Cloudflare under its own retention periods.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When we no longer need information, we delete it or make it anonymous.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>We use encrypted connections (HTTPS with HSTS), strict security headers, spam protection and providers with strong security programs. We limit access to the people who need it. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but if a breach affects your personal information, we will notify you and the authorities as the law requires, including under New York's SHIELD Act.</p>

      <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
      <p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Know and access</strong> what personal information we hold about you and get a copy of it.</li>
        <li><strong>Correct</strong> information that is wrong or incomplete.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete</strong> your information, unless we must keep it, for example for tax records.</li>
        <li><strong>Object to or restrict</strong> how we use it, and withdraw any consent you gave.</li>
        <li><strong>Opt out</strong> of marketing email at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Residents of California and other US states with privacy laws, and of the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland, have these rights under their local laws. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
      <p>To make a request, email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a> from the address you used with us. We may ask for information to confirm your identity before we act. You can use an authorized agent, who must show us your signed permission. We reply within 30 days, or 45 days where the law allows, and tell you if we need more time. We won't charge you or treat you differently for using your rights.</p>

      <h2>California notice</h2>
      <p>In the past 12 months we collected these categories of personal information, from you and from your device, for the purposes described above: identifiers (name, email address, IP address), customer records (billing address), commercial information (purchases), internet activity (pages requested), and professional information (company name). We don't collect sensitive personal information, and we disclose these categories only to the service providers listed above.</p>

      <h2>International visitors</h2>
      <p>Benjaire is based in the United States, and our providers process information in the United States and other countries. Where the law requires, they use approved safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework to protect information transferred from the EEA, the UK or Switzerland.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is for businesses and adults and isn't directed to children under 16. We don't knowingly collect their information. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, email us and we will delete it.</p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>Our site links to other sites, including Benjaire brand sites and providers such as Stripe and Calendly. Their privacy practices are their own, so please read their policies.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy as our services or the law change. The date at the top shows when it last changed. If we make a significant change, we will say so on this page before it takes effect.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or requests about privacy: <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>, {SITE.legalName}, New York, NY.</p>
      <LegalDraft />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
